      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The outside-view base rate is the January\u2013July first-print mean: (0.1 + 0.2 - 0.1 + 0.5 + 0.3 + 0.3 + 0.0)/7 = 0.185714%. The reference class spans a contraction, a strong rebound, and a flat month. Conditioning on an available advance estimate uses the paired advance-to-first-print errors from those same months."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "web.run",
        "call": "Fetch the official monthly GDP table and July release's industry details.",
        "result": "The table reports July all-industries output of 2,371,771 million chained 2017 dollars. The July release reports construction +1.3%, retail trade -1.0%, manufacturing -0.9%, and petroleum refineries -6.2%, with unplanned refinery downtime contributing to the refinery decline. Sources: https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/tbl1/en/tv.action?pid=3610043401 ; https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/daily-quotidien/260929/dq260929a-eng.htm ."
