      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level: July's output level establishes the denominator, without an independent growth adjustment. Momentum: the historical mean supplies the prior, while August's +0.2% advance supplies current-month information. One-off effects: anticipated retail and mining gains and extraction losses are already incorporated in that advance; refinery recovery remains an upside scenario. Policy mechanism: no separately quantified policy adjustment is supported by the fetched evidence. Combining these components therefore adds only the empirically estimated advance-to-first-print bias."
