        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use an empirical advance-plus-error model, anchored first on the seven January\u2013July initial growth prints. Because this is a change series, dispersion is calculated from the growth values themselves: squared deviations sum to 0.248571; sigma = 0.203540 percentage points = sqrt(0.248571/6); the unconditional 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 0.260531. Update the 0.185714% base rate to the August advance of 0.2%, then add the historical mean first-minus-advance error, 0.4/7 = 0.057143, giving 0.257143%. Paired-error squared deviations sum to 0.057143, so sigma_error = sqrt(0.057143/6) = 0.097590 and 1.28*sigma_error = 0.124915. Allow for estimation uncertainty using an 80% Student-t prediction interval with six degrees of freedom: half-width = 1.439756*0.097590*sqrt(1+1/7) = 0.150207. This is 0.577 times the unconditional half-width; narrowing below 0.75 times is justified by the known August advance and the substantially smaller fetched advance-to-first-print error dispersion. The method assumes those errors remain exchangeable. Implied bounds are 0.106936% and 0.407350%; rounding the forecast fields to four decimals gives point 0.2571%, ciLow 0.1069%, and ciHigh 0.4073%."
